year: 2026
repository-code: "https://github.com/<PLACEHOLDER-USERNAME>/INBMG-Narmada-Basin-Monitoring"
abstract: >
  INBMG (Intelligent Narmada Basin Monitoring & Governance) is a student-led
  research and documentation project developed at IIT Jodhpur, with guidance
  from Dr. Priyank J. Sharma, Department of Civil Engineering, IIT Indore.
  This repository documents the project's evolution from an initial broad
  conceptual vision to its currently implemented technical component: a
  2025 remote-sensing analysis of the Omkareshwar and Maheshwar stretches
  of the Narmada River using Sentinel-2 multispectral imagery and Google
  Earth Engine, computing eight spectral indices (NDTI, NDWI, MNDWI, AWEI,
  FAI, NDVI, BSI, TSM) for river-health assessment.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - river health monitoring
  - Narmada River
  - Google Earth Engine
  - Sentinel-2
  - geospatial analysis
  - environmental monitoring
